TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed checkpoint cp-weights because the fixed checkpoint command mutates tracked files by design, which the spec-build driver forbids for a checkpoint lane: the underlying staging actually succeeded (gate node cp-weights returned verdict pass, exitCode 0, and both receipts report the expected 131 shards / 185563854698 bytes), but scripts/stage-weights-both.sh installs each node's freshly generated receipt over the tracked paths results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json and results/receipts/weights-worker.json, so the only surviving delta against base 1e2eef72397ee0a8053ed816a70e25e55e7aa304 is the rewritten \"ts\" field (2026-08-29T12:47:30 -> 2026-08-30T07:08:43 and 2026-08-30T07:06:56). The driver saw those dirty tracked files and exited 1 with \"spec-build-driver: checkpoint command changed tracked files instead of validating the prepared base\"; the accompanying result-projection-timeout (finalMessage not projected within 10000 ms) is a downstream consequence of that non-zero exit, not an independent machinery fault. This is deterministic and will recur on every re-run: install_receipt unconditionally mv's the staged receipt into the tracked results/receipts tree, and stage-weights.sh stamps a wall-clock \"ts\" each invocation, so a byte-for-byte identical staging still produces a tracked-file change. The cause lies outside this task's authority — cp-weights is a checkpoint whose argv is fixed by the worklist and whose brief forbids repository modification, so no edit inside this lane can stop the command from dirtying the tree, and retry is barred for checkpoint tasks in any case. Compounding this, overseer steering comment 2 instructs lanes to always land a non-empty RECONCILE note, which is the exact opposite of the checkpoint contract the driver is enforcing here; that note should be scoped to spec-build lanes only, since following it on cp-weights guarantees the same failure. The fix belongs in the staging scripts (or the checkpoint gate contract): make receipt installation idempotent so an unchanged staging leaves the tracked receipt untouched, for example by omitting or normalizing the volatile \"ts\" field, or by comparing the staged receipt against the tracked one and skipping the mv when the substantive payload matches, or by directing per-run receipts to an untracked/ignored location with only a validating comparison against the committed baseline. Note also that the 2026-08-30 revision title asserts the artifact has no catalog row and requires a fresh ~185.6 GB copy per node; the equal shard and byte counts indicate the re-copy did complete, so the operator only needs the write-path change, not a re-plan of the staging work itself.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","goal":"Make the both-node weights staging checkpoint idempotent against the tracked working tree so that a successful, unchanged re-stage validates the prepared base without modifying any tracked file, allowing checkpoint cp-weights to pass under the spec-build driver's no-tracked-change contract while still failing loudly on a genuine staging error.","paths":["scripts/stage-weights-both.sh","scripts/stage-weights.sh","results/receipts/weights-coordinator.json","results/receipts/weights-worker.json"],"acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"staging-still-passes","description":"Running the checkpoint command end to end still stages both nodes and exits zero, printing the per-node shard and byte summary and the 'both nodes staged' line.","argv":["bash","scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]},{"id":"tracked-tree-clean-after-run","description":"After a successful run whose staged payload matches the committed receipts, the tracked receipt files are byte-identical to HEAD and git reports no change under results/receipts.","argv":["git","diff","--exit-code","--","results/receipts"]},{"id":"no-untracked-residue","description":"A successful run leaves no new untracked files behind in the repository working tree.","argv":["bash","-lc","test -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\""]},{"id":"failure-still-blocks","description":"A staging receipt whose status is not pass still causes the command to exit non-zero and to quarantine that receipt outside the passing receipt path, so the idempotence change cannot mask a real staging failure.","argv":["bash","-lc","grep -q 'results/receipts/failed' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh && grep -q 'sys.exit(1)' scripts/stage-weights-both.sh"]}]}}
